WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.544 --> 00:00:04.254
What is this place?

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:06.506
It's the everything factory, silly.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:09.300
It’s good to see you, Joseph. How are you?

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.261
Yeah, man! Really good!

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:13.847
Hey, I wanted to tell you because we haven’t had a

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.016
 chance to speak face to face, 

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.476
how good you are in &lt;i&gt;Wolfboy&lt;/i&gt;, man.

00:00:18.476 --> 00:00:20.145
Your performance is really good.

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:21.938
I thought that went very well!

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:24.733
You too. Luxcraft was absolutely incredible.

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.943
Why that’s brilliant!

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:27.819
Whew!

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:29.904
So there’s some pretty cool questions they’ve printed

00:00:29.904 --> 00:00:31.698
on these nifty &lt;i&gt;Wolfboy&lt;/i&gt; cards.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.241
Should we dive into these?

00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:34.534
Oh yeah, I have some too.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.536
We’re going on an adventure!

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.164
What is imagination in your eyes?

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:42.125
My mom was just reminding me that she used to find me

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:45.503
playing alone in my room with all kinds of

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:48.214
just made up characters and stories and stuff,

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.340
and she would ask me what I was doing,

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.302
and I would say I’m playing with my imagination.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.262
That was not the answer I was expecting.

00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:56.306
&lt;i&gt;(Laughing)&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:59.267
What do you do to get your creative juices flowing?

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:03.146
I just like sitting down in my armchair and just

00:01:03.688 --> 00:01:05.440
staring at a drawing pad thinking,

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.734
what can I draw?

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:09.736
What could be cool?

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.905
So you draw? I didn’t know this about you.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:14.157
Yeah, I like to draw quite frequently.

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:17.202
It’s pretty much the best way to 

00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:20.371
get what you see in your mind out.

00:01:20.371 --> 00:01:21.748
Yeah!

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.457
If that makes sense.

00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:23.708
That makes perfect sense.

00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:25.752
It’s, it’s one of the creative skills 

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.254
I’ve always wanted to spend more time with.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.216
Mmm, I see we have some work to do

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:35.804
What is an idea that no one else has come up with yet?

00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:37.472
Ooh ooh, I have an idea

00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:38.056
Great!

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:42.560
A time traveling elevator? Or a magical slide!

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.730
 It’s a clock that can rewind time,

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.482
so if you miss your alarm,

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:51.778
you can just pull back the clock handle and rewind time.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.530
So you never end up being late.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.116
I need that for sure.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.117
&lt;i&gt;(laughing)&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.576
Such little respect for time!

00:01:58.576 --> 00:01:59.702
&lt;i&gt;(laughing)&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:59.702 --> 00:02:02.205
What’s the strangest dream you’ve ever had?

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:04.207
I was in the ocean,

00:02:04.582 --> 00:02:08.253
and for some reason, I could just tell I was a fish.

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:11.381
Yet, I still had human arms and legs.

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:12.173
Mhmm.

00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:14.342
And then I found some other fish and

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:17.428
I then started talking to them for some reason.

00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:18.888
Do you remember the conversations?

00:02:18.888 --> 00:02:22.392
It sounded like English, but for some reason,

00:02:22.392 --> 00:02:25.937
everyone else was speaking in like,

00:02:25.937 --> 00:02:27.230
just, they were just going--

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:30.191
&lt;i&gt;(fish noises)&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:30.191 --> 00:02:31.734
I don’t even know how that happened.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:32.652
It was so weird.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.653
&lt;i&gt;(laughing)&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.614
It’s all a dream!

00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:39.576
How much fun was it playing Professor Luxcraft?

00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:42.745
I had so much fun playing Luxcraft.

00:02:42.745 --> 00:02:43.413
Cool!

00:02:43.413 --> 00:02:45.832
As an actor, one of the big thrills for me

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.793
is getting to play somebody that’s different from myself.

00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:53.923
Luxcraft is this like big guy with a huge, purple beard

00:02:53.923 --> 00:02:56.676
and he can do magic and he’s so wise.

00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:58.803
Be one with the wisps.

00:02:58.803 --> 00:03:01.139
Let them connect to your creativity.

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:02.557
Over the course of playing him,

00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:05.351
I sort of found things about him like,

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.062
oh, actually, that’s sort of like me.

00:03:08.062 --> 00:03:10.023
Being an artist is sort of like being

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.566
a wizard in certain ways.

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:15.153
I knew it! I knew it! Ha ha!

00:03:15.153 --> 00:03:18.698
When people watch &lt;i&gt;Wolfboy and the Everything Factory,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:21.576
what is it that you hope they get out of it?

00:03:21.951 --> 00:03:24.579
One of the best parts about playing Sprout was

00:03:24.579 --> 00:03:26.956
the message he was bringing out to people,

00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:30.043
which is do not let your fears control what you do

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.295
and I found that very helpful.

00:03:32.295 --> 00:03:36.007
Just be yourself. Make us proud, okay?

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:38.968
&lt;i&gt;(babbles)&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.595
It’s a real pleasure talking to you.

00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:44.224
Yeah, it was absolutely amazing finally getting to meet you.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.475
I hope to see you again soon.

00:03:45.475 --> 00:03:47.518
Alright, thanks Archie. Good talking to you, man.

00:03:47.518 --> 00:03:50.480
Alright. Bye Joseph!

